  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Figure 15, 'How digital signature verification works'. The upper panel, Document Signing, repeats Figure 14: document, document hash, signed with the private key, signed hash added to the document to make the DDCC:VS. The signer sends the digitally signed document and the public key to the verifier. The lower panel, Document Validation: the verifier calculates a hash from the document and, using the public key, obtains the hash from the signed hash; the two values are compared, and a matching hash indicates a valid document, one that contains the information that was signed with the private key.",
